Z||000000||PaUL||04-09-99||08:00 PM||||Hey all, I found a great parts site, they got all kinds of parts not just for Fieros. I was looking for ball joints and this place lists parts from 4 different manufacturers: Moog, TRW, Perfect Circle, and MCQUAY NORRIS <br>. Their prices beat those Fiero specialty places, they list the front lower balljoints for less than $20! When I changed one of my fronts, the local parts store here charged me over $30 for a Moog balljoint. Heres the URL:  http://www.fastpartsonline.com/<br>check it out, you wont be disappointed<br>
Z||000001||theogre||04-10-99||08:03 PM||||i've found almost anyplace is cheaper than Fiero store, FOCOA, etc, when it comes to standard parts. Rememeber, Fiero is a GM car, and many GM cars share parts with it. Enigne, breaks, suspension, and other areas all have standard GM parts in them.<p>Strauss Discount Auto (formerly R&S Strauss), PepBoys, AutoZone, should all be checked first for parts before going to FOCOA, Fiero Store, etc. Your local speed shop, and AmsOil deallers should be checked as well. All speed shops can get K&N, and AmsOil still caries Fiero oiled foam air cleaners. (AmsOil air cleaners for 4cyl are about 25$us. About 10$ less than K&N, and are less likely to crush/deform than K&N, Fram, Purolator, etc.)
